:EmrakulThePromisedEnd rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  :Card ;
    :cardName "Emrakul, the Promised End" ;
    :manaCost "{13}" ;
    :manaValue "13"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    :hasSuperType :Legendary ;
    :hasCardType :Creature ;
    :hasSubType :Eldrazi ;
    :hasRarity :MythicRare ;
    :isInSet :InnistradRemastered ;
    :cardNumber "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    :artist "Jaime Jones" ;
    :hasLanguage :English ;
    :power "13" ;
    :powerValue "13"^^xsd:integer ;
    :toughness "13" ;
    :toughnessValue "13"^^xsd:integer ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Flying ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Protection ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Trample ;
    :printedText """This spell costs {1} less to cast for each card type among cards in your graveyard.
When you cast this spell, you gain control of target opponent during that player's next turn. After that turn, that player takes an extra turn.
Flying, trample, protection from instants"""@en ;
    :oracleText """This spell costs {1} less to cast for each card type among cards in your graveyard.
When you cast this spell, you gain control of target opponent during that player's next turn. After that turn, that player takes an extra turn.
Flying, trample, protection from instants"""@en ;
    :flavorText """An enigma as vexing as life itself."""@en ;
    :gathererUrl "https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=685819"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :scryfallUrl "https://scryfall.com/card/inr/5/emrakul-the-promised-end"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :hasLegality
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Commander ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Standard ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Modern ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Legacy ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Protection from instants means that Emrakul can’t be the target of instant spells or activated or triggered abilities from instant cards, and damage that would be dealt to it by instant spells or cards is prevented. Instant spells may still affect it in other ways; for example, it would still receive the bonus from Rally the Peasants."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If the targeted player skips their next turn, you’ll control the next turn the affected player actually takes, and the extra turn the player takes will be after that turn."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """While controlling another player, you can see all cards in the game that player can see. This includes cards in that player’s hand, face-down cards that player controls, and any cards in that player’s library the player may look at."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You can use only the affected player’s resources (cards, mana, and so on) to pay costs for that player; you can’t use your own. Similarly, you can use the affected player’s resources only to pay that player’s costs; you can’t spend them on your costs."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """An ability that triggers when a player casts a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered or otherwise leaves the stack without resolving."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You can’t make any illegal decisions or illegal choices—you can’t do anything that player couldn’t do. You can’t make choices or decisions for that player that aren’t called for by the game rules or by any cards, permanents, spells, abilities, and so on. If an effect causes another player to make decisions that the affected player would normally make (such as Master Warcraft does), that effect takes precedence. In other words, if the affected player wouldn’t make a decision, you wouldn’t make that decision on that player’s behalf."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """In a Two-Headed Giant game, gaining control of a player causes you to gain control of each player on that team."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You also can’t make any choices or decisions for the player that would be called for by the tournament rules (such as whether to take an intentional draw or whether to call a judge)."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Protection abilities only apply while the object with the ability is on the battlefield. Notably, Emrakul may be the target of a spell that targets it while on the stack, such as Syncopate."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Controlling a player doesn’t allow you to look at that player’s sideboard. If an effect instructs that player to choose a card from outside the game, you can’t have that player choose any card."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You can’t make the affected player concede. That player may choose to concede at any time, even while you’re controlling that player."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """While controlling another player, you also continue to make your own choices and decisions."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Multiple player-controlling effects that affect the same player overwrite each other. The last one to be created is the one that works. If multiple players have cast Emrakul and targeted the same player, each ability’s effect will create an extra turn."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """While controlling another player, you make all choices and decisions that player is allowed to make or is told to make during that turn. This includes choices about what spells to cast or what abilities to activate, as well as any decisions called for by triggered abilities or for any other reason."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The player you’re controlling is still the active player during that turn."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You only control the player. You don’t control any of that player’s permanents, spells, or abilities."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If the targeted player loses the game while you control their turn during a multiplayer game, the extra turn never begins."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The card types that could appear in your graveyard are artifact, battle, creature, enchantment, instant, kindred, land, planeswalker, and sorcery. Supertypes (such as legendary and basic) and subtypes (such as Human and Equipment) are not counted. The maximum discount that Emrakul’s own ability can provide is {9}."""@en ] .

:WretchedGryff rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  :Card ;
    :cardName "Wretched Gryff" ;
    :manaCost "{7}" ;
    :manaValue "7"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    :hasCardType :Creature ;
    :hasSubType :Eldrazi ;
    :hasSubType :Hippogriff ;
    :hasRarity :Common ;
    :hasColorIdentity :Blue ;
    :isInSet :InnistradRemastered ;
    :cardNumber "7"^^xsd:integer ;
    :artist "Darek Zabrocki" ;
    :hasLanguage :English ;
    :power "3" ;
    :powerValue "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    :toughness "4" ;
    :toughnessValue "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Flying ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Emerge ;
    :printedText """Emerge {5}{U} (You may cast this spell by sacrificing a creature and paying the emerge cost reduced by that creature's mana value.)
When you cast this spell, draw a card.
Flying"""@en ;
    :oracleText """Emerge {5}{U} (You may cast this spell by sacrificing a creature and paying the emerge cost reduced by that creature's mana value.)
When you cast this spell, draw a card.
Flying"""@en ;
    :gathererUrl "https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=685821"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :scryfallUrl "https://scryfall.com/card/inr/7/wretched-gryff"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :hasLegality
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Commander ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Standard ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Modern ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Legacy ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You may sacrifice a creature with mana value greater than or equal to the emerge cost. If you do, you’ll pay only the colored mana component of the emerge cost."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """An ability that triggers when a player casts a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered or otherwise leaves the stack without resolving."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Emerge represents two static abilities that function while the spell with emerge is on the stack. “Emerge [cost]” means “You may cast this spell by paying [cost] and sacrificing a creature rather than paying its mana cost” and “If you chose to pay this spell’s emerge cost, its total cost is reduced by an amount of generic mana equal to the sacrificed creature’s mana value.”"""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """A creature’s mana value is determined solely by the mana symbols printed in its upper right corner (unless that creature is the back face of a double-faced card, is a melded permanent, or is copying something else; see below). If the mana cost includes {X}, X is 0. If it’s a single-faced card with no mana symbols in its upper right corner (because it’s an animated land, for example), its mana value is 0. Ignore any alternative costs or additional costs (such as kicker) that were paid as the creature was cast."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Once you begin to cast a spell with emerge, no player may take actions until you’re done. Notably, opponents can’t try to remove the creature you wish to sacrifice."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Colored mana components of emerge costs can’t be reduced with emerge."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The mana value of a creature spell with emerge isn’t affected by whether its emerge cost is paid. For example, if you cast Decimator of the Provinces for its emerge cost and sacrifice a creature whose mana value is 3, Decimator of the Provinces’s mana value remains 10."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If you cast a spell for another cost “rather than paying its mana cost,” such as an emerge cost, you can’t choose to cast it for any other alternative costs. You can, however, pay additional costs, such as kicker costs. If the spell has any mandatory additional costs, those must be paid to cast it."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If you sacrifice a creature with {X} in its mana cost, that X is 0."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The creature chosen to be sacrificed is still on the battlefield as the cost of the emerge spell is determined and as you activate mana abilities to cast the emerge spell. Its abilities may affect the spell’s cost, be activated to generate mana, and so on. However, if it has an ability that triggers when a spell is cast, it will have been sacrificed before that ability can trigger."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You may sacrifice a creature with a mana value of 0, such as a token creature that’s not a copy of another permanent, to cast a spell for its emerge cost. You’ll just pay the full emerge cost with no reduction."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2025-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The mana value of the back face of a double-faced card is the mana value of its front face. The mana value of a melded permanent is the sum of the mana values of its front faces. A creature that’s a copy of either has a mana value of 0."""@en ] .

